    <main class="page-shell">
      <article class="about-wrap">
        <header class="about-header">
          <p class="eyebrow">Matt McGowan</p>
          <h1 class="about-title">CTO. Engineering Leader. Systems Whisperer.</h1>
        </header>

        <div class="about-body">
          <p>
            I'm Matthew (Matt) McGowan, an infrastructure, SRE, and platform leader running $10M+ programs and production systems, from federal platforms to multi-tenant SaaS on Azure and AWS. Engineers call me the Systems Whisperer: I find what's actually broken in infrastructure, teams, and process, fix it, and explain it in plain English. I've led 50+ people, including vendor teams. I work across SaaS, FinTech, platform companies and regulated infrastructure, including federal and defense, from the architecture decision to the 2am incident call. I'm based in Atlanta Metro / US Southeast and work with clients remotely across the US.
          </p>
          <p>
            Most technology problems are really ownership, process, or visibility problems that show up as a bill, an outage, or a stalled roadmap. I fix the system underneath, not just the symptom.
          </p>
          <p>
            I'm the Founder &amp; Chief Technology Officer of NullorNaN Systems. NullorNaN grew out of my freelance fractional CTO work. I launched it full-time in March 2026 and incorporated it in April. It is the practice for my fractional CTO and C2C engineering engagements, and it builds its own SaaS products: NullSig, NullCard and NullPortal, a control panel for fractional leaders that we first built for our own use. Through NullorNaN we offer fractional executive leadership under <a href="https://nullornan.com/nullcxo/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Null CXO</a>, which covers CTO, CIO, CISO or COO seats, hands-on engineering under <a href="https://nullornan.com/null-engineer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Null Engineer</a>, and engineering advisory under <a href="https://nullornan.com/null-advisory/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Null Advisory</a>. Since August 2026 I have served as Fractional CTO and Executive Advisor to Speedmax, through NullorNaN. I'm also a member of the Go Fractional vetted network.
          </p>
          <p>
            Recent NullorNaN work: I led a NIST CSF 2.0 self-assessment of NullPortal and its Cloudflare edge across all six functions, mapping 40 gaps to SOC 2 and PCI DSS, then ran a SOC 2 readiness check from there. I'm leading an agentic engineering overhaul: one agent flags code and cloud security risks, another opens the pull request, and nothing merges without human approval. For a Confidential Client, I cut Azure spend 50% (about $50K) after finding cloud waste they could not see. That showed their investor the team could manage costs and helped clear the way for a $1M infrastructure investment.
          </p>
          <p>
            From June to November 2026 I served as Co-Founder and Chief Technology &amp; Operations Officer (CTO/COO) of OUR+'R Technologies, a driver-first rideshare platform. OUR+'R started as a NullorNaN advisory client and offered me the co-founder seat. I took product and engineering from concept to a working MVP in one week on Node.js, React, TypeScript and Postgres, built with AI coding agents, and cut build time 60% by moving the platform to Kubernetes. I'm now mostly advisory, by choice.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some results I can share. At Speedmax, I fixed a critical backup failure and I/O wait in about 15 minutes, for a client-reported 45% gain in responsiveness, then consolidated VMs to cut infrastructure costs about 50%.
          </p>
          <p>
            From January 2021 to March 2026 I worked full-time on one $10M defense (DoD) program in Peachtree City, GA, under three employers: IBSS, then Broadleaf, Inc. after a prime transition, then ASRC Federal after it acquired Broadleaf.
          </p>
          <p>
            At IBSS (January 2021 to October 2022) I was Linux/Unix SME and Platform Lead (Senior Systems Administrator), hired for a large-scale global deployment across 70+ sites. I scaled the platform from 12 to 120 physical systems in 90 days while remediating 300+ security findings, and kept delivery on track through an unannounced DoD Command Cyber Readiness Inspection (CCRI) in the final 20 days. I raised uptime from 85% to 99% with Ansible automation, cut patching after ACAS scans from 6 business days to 6 hours, and cut operating spend 35 to 40%. I led the Puppet, Ansible and Chef evaluation for the client CIO, which made Ansible the standard. Toward the end of that role I began taking on early engineering-manager duties; the official title did not change.
          </p>
          <p>
            At Broadleaf, Inc. (October 2022 to April 2023) I was Engineering Manager / Technical PM (Linux Senior System Administrator). I brought the Linux fleet into the program's on-prem to Azure migration, installing Azure agents and aligning Linux with Active Directory and Entra ID. I built the platform on Zero Trust principles, tying RBAC to Active Directory and Microsoft Entra ID with least-privilege access, and started a Zero Trust initiative to bring the Linux platform up to federal executive order standards. I cut maintenance and patching windows from three weekends, often running over, to one day. I served as the escalation point for complex production incidents and hired two senior Linux engineers.
          </p>
          <p>
            At ASRC Federal (April 2023 to March 2026) I was Engineering Manager / Technical PM (Senior Systems Administrator), managing engineering on a $10M defense program supporting 50 schools and 20,000+ students at DoDEA. The contract labor category never changed because the role modification couldn't be secured on the contract. I led 25 engineers across 3 divisions (12 reports) and 70+ sites and cut outage recovery time 75%, from 60 to 15 minutes. I oversaw the zero-downtime rebuild of 112 Linux servers, coordinating engineering and Cyber Security, secured and ran a 24-month AI strategy, raised operations visibility from 50% to 90% of projects, supported the program's move into Azure, and owned SLOs and postmortems.
          </p>
          <p>
            From July 2019 to December 2025 I worked freelance as an Engineering Systems Analyst and Fractional CTO, giving startups and SMBs senior technology leadership without a full-time hire. I took fractional CTO and CIO engagements in gaming, dating, infrastructure and cloud hosting, on weekends alongside full-time roles. I brought a Confidential Client's runaway AI spend under control in 30 days with AI governance, and cut another client's Kubernetes costs 30% by consolidating 10 clusters to 4. I designed and built CastleGuard, an RBAC platform for Minecraft game servers, publicly released in 2021 and now open source. Private versions grew early-access MRR from $300 to a $4,000 monthly average. I also built a media relay system for esports events. Before that, I worked at Aptum, RamNode and INTERNET NETWORKS.
          </p>
          <p>
            Frameworks I work with hands-on: SOC 2 and PCI DSS readiness, NIST CSF 2.0 readiness self-assessments, and a live DoD Command Cyber Readiness Inspection (CCRI).
          </p>
          <p>
            I write the Null vs the Stack series. I'm open to Director-and-above leadership roles where I stay hands-on, or senior technical roles at Staff and Principal level, and I take select fractional CTO and C2C work through NullorNaN Systems. Fit and impact matter more to me than the exact title.
          </p>

          <!-- Longer versions of the home page pull-quotes. Verified word for word from public LinkedIn recommendations. Never reword; trim only at whole sentence boundaries. -->
          <figure>
            <blockquote>
              <p>"Matthew provided an extraordinary impact to our business when we needed it most. We first contacted Matthew when we were having a serious reliability issue affecting our entire business operation on a large scale level. Matthew was able to fix in 15 minutes what several others were unable to solve in weeks, and provided several realistic paths forward to permanent resolution. After that, he has provided ongoing advisory level assistance with ongoing virtualization issues and strategy."</p>
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>Dani Perteet, Founder, Speedmax (LinkedIn recommendation)</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <blockquote>
              <p>"He transitioned us from a solo-built MVP to an enterprise-grade 'Production Dev' environment on DigitalOcean in record time, always prioritizing redundancy and multi-region failover. What sets Matt apart is his ability to bridge deep Platform Engineering expertise with a sharp operational mind. He doesn't just build code; he builds a 'Technical Fortress.' If you are looking for an executive who leads with integrity, data-backed logic, and a zero-downtime mentality, Matthew is the gold standard. I couldn't ask for a better partner to lead our technical and operational scale."</p>
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption>Clayton Hill, MBA, Founder and CEO, OUR+'R Technologies, Inc. (LinkedIn recommendation)</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <p class="about-routing">
            For fractional or advisory work, start at <a href="https://nullornan.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">nullornan.com</a> or <a href="https://app.reclaim.ai/m/nullornan/lets-talk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">book a free 30-minute call</a>.
            For full-time roles or a direct connection, find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthewcmcgowan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.
          </p>
